The '''Mines of Divan''' is a location in the {{Zone|Crystal Hollows}}, more specifically the {{Zone|Mithril Deposits}}, where the {{Item|Jade Crystal}} can be obtained. Claiming the crystal requires a {{Item|Scavenged Emerald Hammer}}, {{Item|Scavenged Diamond Axe}}, {{Item|Scavenged Lapis Sword}}, and a {{Item|Scavenged Golden Hammer}}. Because these items are Quest items, they aren't able to be traded. Using a {{Item|Wishing Compass}} in the {{Zone|Mithril Deposits}} before obtaining a {{Item|Jade Crystal}} points to the Mines of Divan.

{{ZoneText|Fear entering the mines.|The dwarves delved too greedily and too deep.|Treasures piled high, who knows what lies beneath.}}

== Purpose ==
Talking to any {{NPCSprite|Keepers of Divan;Keeper}} gives the player a {{Item|Metal Detector}}. While holding the Metal Detector, the player's distance from the treasure is shown, as well as increasingly louder/higher pitched beeps when nearing treasure. The treasure chest can contain certain items, including a Scavenged Item. The {{Item|Jade Crystal}} will appear in the center after delivering each Scavenged Item to their respective keepers. As you won't get Scavenged Items you already have in your inventory, you need to find 22.22 treasures on average to get one Crystal.  

The treasure chest can reward either one of four [[Scavenged Items]] (18%), {{Item|Mithril Powder}} (8%), {{Item|Gemstone Powder}} (6%), (4x, 8x, 16x, 32x or 64x) Rough {{Item|Gemstone}}s (68%), and a rare chance of obtaining a {{Item|Pickonimbus 2000}} (0.06%) or 2x Fine {{Item|Gemstone}}s (0.01%).

